caption: Tree Profile

The following GATES adaptation shows how a Shadow Arts institutional tree can represent Water Breathing as a lineage of fixed sword Jutsu. The visible water is presentation unless a particular Jutsu explicitly creates a physical effect. Forms One through Ten are ordinary tree material. Eleventh Form: Dead Calm is shown as a later Secret Master Technique appended by a mastered Shadow Doyen. Raw and Final values are positive penalty magnitudes; Tier 2 Cost is Final Jutsu Penalty + 1 CP.

Tree Profile — Water Breathing

Style Weapons: One sword. Every Jutsu whose authored delivery is a sword attack requires a ready sword and uses that sword's ordinary legal attack mode. The profile does not turn self-buff-only forms into weapon attacks and does not let another weapon substitute for the sword.

Style Armor: Unrestricted. Water Breathing has no tree-wide armor prohibition in this GATES instance.

Required Implements: A sword for every sword-delivery Jutsu; self-buff-only Jutsu may be used while disarmed when their own text permits it.

Tree Advantages: All Universal Shadow Arts Conditioning. Derived permissions are Super Jump 1 after purchasing Water Wheel; Enhanced Parry (Sword) +1 after purchasing Drop Ripple Thrust; and Perfect Balance and Catfall after purchasing Splashing Water Flow, Turbulent.
